===== Hardware Mods =====
==== USB Mod ====
** Required materials **
  * 1 x LM7805 (Voltage regulator, consider a step-down model)
  * 1 x Electrolytic capacitor 10-470uF 25V
  * 2 x Resistors 4K7 0,25W
  * 1 x USB Connector
{{media:comtrend:ct-5813:ct-5813_board_up_usb.jpg?400}}
{{media:comtrend:ct-5813:ct-5813_usb_mod_possible.jpg?250x350}}

You need to add a 4K7 resistor on the other side of the board:\\
{{media:comtrend:ct-5813:ct-5813_board_down_usb.jpg?400}}

==== Overclocking ====

The CPU is configured as default to operate at 400 MHz. With this mod it will be configured to operate at 533 MHz. Solder three 4.7 kohm resistors as shown in the picture.

{{:media:comtrend:ct-5813:wap-5813n-overclocking_533.jpg?direct&400|}}


